-names></name></person-group><source>Cybernetics: or Control and Communication in the Animal and Machine</source><year>1948</year><publisher-loc>Cambridge</publisher-loc><publisher-name>MIT Press</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="R26"><label>26</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ivanov</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Pal</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dougherty</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dynamics preserving size reduction mappings for probabilistic Boolean networks</article-title><source>IEEE Trans. Signal Process</source><year>2007</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>2310</fpage><lpage>2322</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R27"><label>27</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Feldman</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>CTS: a new discipline to catalyze the transfer of information</article-title><source>CTS Clin. Transl. Sci</source><year>2008</year><volume>1</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>2</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R28"><label>28</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wiener</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosenblueth</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The mathematical formation of the problem of conduction of impulses in a network of connected excitable elements, specifically in cardiac muscle</article-title><source>Arch. Inst. Cardiol Mexico</source><year>1946</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>204</fpage><lpage>265</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="R29"><label>29</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hanczar</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Hua</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Dougherty</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decorrelation of the true and estimated classifier errors in high-dimensional settings</article-title><source>EURASIP J. Bioinform. Syst. Biol</source><year>2007</year><comment>Article ID 38473, 12 pages</comment></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. (1)</label><caption><p>Steady-state distribution of GRN: (a) original network; (b) with intervention.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="CG-10-102_F1"/></fig></floats-group></article>